{
  "$schema": "https://aka.ms/codetour-schema",
  "title": "Deployment flow: queueing, the checks gate, and the Agent handoff",
  "description": "Follows one Deploy from its refusals, through the Agent handoff, to the state changes that end it. Covers ENG-108.",
  "steps": [
    {
      "file": "janus-go/internal/services/fleet/deployments.go",
      "line": 218,
      "title": "Refusals come first",
      "description": "`func (s *Service) queue`. Every refusal is checked here, before anything is recorded: the Build, its Check and the Agent."
    },
    {
      "file": "janus-go/internal/services/fleet/deployments.go",
      "line": 249,
      "title": "Up-front Agent check",
      "description": "`s.ready(`. The Agent must be connected and not paused before a Deployment is queued."
    },
    {
      "file": "janus-go/internal/services/fleet/link.go",
      "line": 199,
      "title": "What ready checks",
      "description": "`func (s *Service) ready`. It reads what the Agent last reported over its connection: paused, offline, or ready."
    },
    {
      "file": "janus-go/internal/services/fleet/deployments.go",
      "line": 290,
      "title": "The Deployment runs in the background",
      "description": "`func (s *Service) run`. A goroutine the service owns hands the Deployment to its Agent until the Agent reports it healthy or refuses it."
    },
    {
      "file": "janus-go/internal/services/fleet/deployments.go",
      "line": 299,
      "title": "Queued to starting",
      "description": "`string(deployments.Queued)`. The first move of the state machine, a compare and swap in fleet.db."
    },
    {
      "file": "janus-go/internal/services/fleet/deployments.go",
      "line": 157,
      "title": "The Agent handoff",
      "description": "`s.sendToAgent(`. The module and its limits go to the Agent as a Deploy command."
    },
    {
      "file": "janus-go/internal/services/fleet/link.go",
      "line": 180,
      "title": "The command reaches the Agent",
      "description": "`func (s *Service) sendToAgent`. It checks the Owner has the Agent, sends the command over the Agent link, and maps unreachable and refused to errors."
    },
    {
      "file": "janus-go/internal/services/fleet/deployments.go",
      "line": 336,
      "title": "Every failure ends here",
      "description": "`func (s *Service) fail`. It moves the Deployment to failed from whichever state it is in, with its own context."
    },
    {
      "file": "janus-go/internal/domain/deployments/deployments.go",
      "line": 40,
      "title": "The state machine",
      "description": "`func CanMove` says which moves are legal. The transitions themselves are listed in the machine map just above it."
    },
    {
      "file": "janus-go/internal/services/fleet/store.go",
      "line": 269,
      "title": "Compare and swap in SQLite",
      "description": "`func (s *Service) moveDeployment`. The move happens only while the Deployment is still in the state the caller saw."
    },
    {
      "file": "janus-go/internal/services/fleet/store.go",
      "line": 69,
      "title": "The one-in-flight rule in the schema",
      "description": "`CREATE UNIQUE INDEX one_inflight_deployment_per_project`. Two Deployments of one Project cannot be queued or starting at once."
    }
  ]
}
